@startuml topologia-hub-mesh
title Topología Hub-Mesh: Flujo de Configuración y Datos

participant "Peer A" as PA
participant "Orchestrator" as Orch
participant "Hub Agent" as Hub
participant "Peer B" as PB

note over PA, PB
  **Hub-Mesh** (híbrida)
  HUB como bootstrap + relay de fallback.
  Peers intentan conexión directa; si falla, relay via HUB.
end note

PA -> Orch : config.get_peer_config
Orch --> PA : {peer: HUB, direct_peers: [B]}
note right of PA
  wg0.conf genera:
  - [Peer] para HUB (relay fallback)
  - [Peer] para B (directo)
end note

PB -> Orch : config.get_peer_config
Orch --> PB : {peer: HUB, direct_peers: [A]}
note right of PB
  wg0.conf genera:
  - [Peer] para HUB (relay fallback)
  - [Peer] para A (directo)
end note

PA -> PA : probe_direct_peers()
PA -> Orch : peer.report_reachability("A", "B", reachable=true/false)

alt reachable == true
    PA -> PB : tráfico directo WireGuard
else reachable == false
    PA -> Hub : tráfico via wg-HUB (relay)
    Hub -> PB : reenvía via wg-HUB
end

note over PA, PB
  **Características**:
  - 1-2 saltos (directo o via HUB)
  - Intenta directo primero (baja latencia)
  - Si NAT bloquea, relay via HUB (funciona siempre)
  - probe_direct_peers monitorea handshakes
  - Orchestrator clasifica peers: direct vs relay_only
end note

@enduml
